    {
        "content": "<p>This problem is summarized (the right can be decomposed by the square difference formula) and then analyzes the content of 2^(2^(n-1))+1 prime factor 2 (the highest power divisible by 2) to prove that the order of 2 modulo p is 2^n, and introduces 2^n divisible p-1 If there are two prime factors, it is done, if it is a prime number, then the Euler function is 2^(2^(n-1)), and the remaining case ≥ 2n is only ≥ 2nd power of the prime number</p>",
        "id": 479716131,
