    {
        "content": "<p>Hi, I'm using Claude in a lean project that uses NumberField.InfiniteAdeleRing K and ran into the problem that Nontrivial (InfiniteAdeleRing K) has no instance in Mathlib registered (yet?). I saw that the FLT project is using InfiniteAdeleRing a lot but I could not find the basic instance there, either. As InfiniteAdeleRing K = Π v : InfinitePlace K, v.Completion and each v.Completion is either ℝ or ℂ (both are nontrivial), doesn't this follow from Pi.instNontrivial [Nonempty (InfinitePlace K)]  if it holds for [NumberField K]? Was this left out intentionally? If not, would a small PR be welcome? <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110038\">@Kevin Buzzard</span></p>",
        "id": 595464150,
        "sender_full_name": "Florian Patzke",
        "timestamp": 1778920489
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What do you need this nontriviality for?</p>",
        "id": 595474311,
        "sender_full_name": "Filippo A. E. Nuccio",
        "timestamp": 1778928577
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I need (0 : AdeleRing ℤ ℚ) ≠ 1, i.e., one_ne_zero for AdeleRing ℤ ℚ. Since AdeleRing is a non-trivial CommRing, the absence of a nontrivial instance blocks standard ring lemmas that require it. I'm trying to connect one of my Lean experiment to Connes' adèle-based approach to RH. Specifically, I want to show that (0 : AdeleRing ℤ ℚ) ≠ 1 as part of establishing that 𝔸_ℚ is a non-trivial substrate for the construction.</p>",
        "id": 595477144,
        "sender_full_name": "Florian Patzke",
        "timestamp": 1778930649
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1080422\">Florian Patzke</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/number.20theory/near/595464150\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Was this left out intentionally?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NumberField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NumberField</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nontrivial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">InfiniteAdeleRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- InfiniteAdeleRing.instNontrivial K</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=NumberField.InfiniteAdeleRing.instNontrivial#doc\">docs#NumberField.InfiniteAdeleRing.instNontrivial</a></p>",
        "id": 595487220,
